src/math.js retains QUICKSCOPER's column-major matrices, vectors, seeded RNG
and slab ray/AABB intersection implementation.
src/mesh.js adapts QUICKSCOPER's expanded-cube mesh builder and batching.

All other browser game runtime files are authored for AFTER//ZERO. The server hosting scaffold uses the maintained Sites Vinext starter and its dependency licenses. Campaign maps, story,
robot/weapon/world designs, UI and synthesized audio contain no imported
proprietary game assets. Donor attribution is provenance, not endorsement.

LibreQuake informed held-fire and weapon-cycling concepts only. No LibreQuake code or assets are included. All optics are original canvas and procedural geometry.

VANILLAJS (QSOLKCB), reviewed at commit
7413d0a9b3555e47a97fbcf344718b42d7ec0f2d, informed projectile lifetime,
chronological-impact and frame-rate regression scenarios. No VANILLAJS source
modules or assets are bundled; AFTER//ZERO retains its own robot hit geometry
and implements its own network timing and compensation.
